{"type":"item.started","item":{"id":"item_6","type":"command_execution","command":"/bin/bash -lc \"cat > review_verify.py <<'PY'\nimport json\nsrc=[dict(id='S-timeout-contract',file='config.go',start_line=149,end_line=161,kind='interface_statement'),dict(id='S-lease-contract',file='config.go',start_line=201,end_line=205,kind='interface_statement'),dict(id='S-config-validation',file='config.go',start_line=333,end_line=385,kind='code_observation'),dict(id='S-get-config',file='api.go',start_line=897,end_line=904,kind='code_observation')]\na='af1bb814fce843fa8230004036da7120'\nitems=[dict(target_id='O-verify-after-majority',aspect='applicability',status='no_issue_found',source_ids=['S-verify-api','S-suffrage','S-api','S-timeout-contract','S-lease-contract','S-config-validation','S-bootstrap','S-config-append','S-membership'],rationale='Reviewed the fixed claim and API comments against the executed configuration. VerifyLeader promises current leadership for avoiding stale FSM reads; nonvoters do not establish election or commitment authority. The antecedent is a completed uniquely identified Apply on B in entry term 3 before invocation on A in term 2, with unchanged three-voter configuration and B-C connectivity. It is stronger than merely observing two local Leader states. Config timing comments define node-local timers, and ValidateConfig enforces local lease<=heartbeat and election>=heartbeat, all met here; no cited uniform cross-node timeout precondition was found. The lease controls eventual local step-down, not an exception allowing successful post-majority-progress VerifyLeader. The harness uses no restore or forced recovery path that would change the contract.',limitations=['Scoped to crash-free in-memory stores and the declared heterogeneous timing configuration.','No claim about all fault schedules or an actual caller read.'],counterevidence=[]),dict(target_id='O-verify-after-majority',aspect='decomposition',status='no_issue_found',source_ids=['S-verify-api','S-verify-start','S-verify-count','S-verify-consume','S-notify','S-heartbeat','S-lease','S-peers','S-replicate-loop'],rationale='The obligation is a necessary public-completion condition, not a claim that lack of voter response must cause immediate error or that pending is success. A completed nil result after independently established higher-term majority progress directly falsifies the selected API condition. It does not depend on proving that every possible stale read or consensus divergence is prevented. Sources show voter-only quorumSize but registration on all replication workers, boolean vote callbacks without suffrage and nil completion after threshold. Lease, negative notification and higher-term ordinary RPC paths are actual alternatives; the fixed harness leaves them running and partitions delivery instead of suppressing their code. The already observed success is attributed at the API endpoint; nonvoter counting remains the supported cause interpretation without a separate counterfactual cause-isolation claim.',limitations=['Does not establish the sufficiency of VerifyLeader for every read protocol, or a consensus log-safety violation.','One completed violating operation does not establish reproducibility under every timing choice.'],counterevidence=[]),dict(target_id=a,aspect='checker_correspondence',status='no_issue_found',source_ids=['S-bootstrap','S-config-append','S-membership','S-startup','S-inmem-partition','S-replicate-loop','S-heartbeat','S-notify','S-verify-start','S-verify-count','S-verify-consume','S-api','S-consume','S-fsm-rest','S-mock-fsm','S-get-config'],rationale='Inspected fixed plan.json and assurance_generated_test.go for artifact af1bb814fce843fa8230004036da7120, plus raw stdout and CheckRun f3ad8013413542dd8759d95a1e2347b5. Real NewRaft/bootstrap/AddNonvoter/AddVoter and Apply construct the prefix; no protocol state is assigned. Successful responses come from real handlers. Optional pipeline support is disabled through the supported interface error; ordinary and heartbeat workers remain independent and active. Each voter path has a failed post-partition call (B/C append counts 5, heartbeat counts 1), so its earlier sequential callbacks completed before target registration. The transport rejects crossing/new partition replies, and there is no snapshot transfer in this noncompacted prefix. The driver then observes B Apply success at stored entry index 8, term 3, command majority-after-partition, versus original term 2. Alias references explicitly chain prefix to drain to majority to invoked; admission_alias is invoked. Result correlation uses independent history and operation fields, not success or changing term. Exactly one target result is present, success=true/error empty after the invocation, so assertion success=false is violated. Future.Error is actually awaited; helpers fail construction on timeout without manufacturing an error result. Shutdown is independent of the forbidden outcome. Connected verification also completed before partition. The process passing reflects measurement completion, not property holds. Supplementary configuration_index=0 comes from GetConfiguration populating only latest configuration and is neither an admission filter nor evidence of a stable index; successful membership futures, subsequent Apply and propagated configurations establish this prefix. FSM counts 1 versus 2 are observations only, not an application-read oracle.',limitations=['Direct callback vote site is not separately instrumented; public endpoint comparison does not require unique cause attribution.','No network/persistent backend, arbitrary schedule, or application-read generalization.'],counterevidence=[])]\nr=json.load(open('../research.json'));cid=r['candidates'][0]['id']\nfeedback=dict(ref_ids=[cid,a,'f3ad8013413542dd8759d95a1e2347b5','S-verify-api','S-verify-start','S-notify'],answered='The fixed formal run observed the complete public API counterexample: B term-3 Apply at index 8 completed before A term-2 VerifyLeader returned nil. This review finds no issue in the scoped applicability, necessity or correspondence; controller assessment determines attribution. Configuration index zero is a supplementary API observation and does not support the oracle.',remaining=['Counterfactual cause isolation and application read behavior are not established; neither is required for this bounded API proposition.'],understanding='unchanged',rationale='Existing map already contains reusable registration, callback and authority mechanisms. Do not copy execution results into facts. Frontier comparison: extending this witness to caller reads adds consequence detail but not a needed premise; pipeline future call ordering has an explicit independent interface expectation and can use an actual transport producer; split vote writes still require a concrete backend fault contract. Select the pipeline consumer contract next.',question_updates={cid:dict(unknowns=['Public endpoint is measured in the fixed check; broader application-read and conflicting-log consequences remain outside scope.','Nonvoter callback causation has source and drain support but no separate counterfactual isolation.'],resume_conditions=[])})\ns=dict(action='review',artifact_id=a,review_items=items,sources=src,feedback=feedback,rationale='Review fixed execution and checker as a whole. The observed violation is a bounded VerifyLeader API result with a real prefix, not a process-failure inference or global consensus conclusion.')\njson.dump(s,open('submission-review-verify.json','w'),indent=2)\nimport jsonschema\njsonschema.validate(s,json.load(open('../submission.schema.json')))\nfrom pathlib import Path\nfor x in src:assert x['end_line']<=len((Path('../agent-source')/x['file']).read_text().splitlines())\nprint('Review schema and citation bounds checked.')\nPY\npython3 review_verify.py\"","aggregated_output":"","exit_code":null,"status":"in_progress"}}
